### 1. Health Liveness Check
GET http://localhost:8000/health
Accept: application/json

### 2. Health Readiness Check (Database connection)
GET http://localhost:8000/health/ready
Accept: application/json

### 3. Register a New User
POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-ID: corr-reg-101

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "StrongPassword123!"
}

### 4. Login (Returns Access Token & Refresh Token)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-ID: corr-login-102

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "StrongPassword123!"
}

### 5. Rotate Refresh Token (Issues new Access & Refresh tokens)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "PASTE_CURRENT_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE"
}

### 6. Demonstrate Token Theft / Reuse Detection
# Re-submitting the previous (already rotated) refresh token will trigger security alert:
# It revokes the entire token family, invalidating all sessions for that family.
POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "PASTE_OLD_ROTATED_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE"
}

### 7. Get Current User Profile (/me)
GET http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
Accept: application/json

### 8. Admin: List All Users (Requires ADMIN or SUPPORT role)
GET http://localhost:8000/api/v1/admin/users?limit=10&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ADMIN_OR_SUPPORT_TOKEN_HERE
Accept: application/json

### 9. Admin: Assign Role (Strictly restricted to ADMIN role)
PATCH http://localhost:8000/api/v1/admin/users/USER_UUID_HERE/role
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "SUPPORT"
}

### 10. Logout and Revoke Access Token JTI
POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/logout?all_sessions=false
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE"
}
